# `kept` is in the hands of code that nobody has seen, so what lies in `inner` is anything, and the record of `make` is what is expected there. `hurry` is no field of that record and nothing above it has the name.
# In `sweep` the read stands in a loop: the looks at the cell pay, and behind them the read finds nothing. In `peek` it stands outside of loops in a function that is not checked, and nobody has written what `inner` holds: the form is withheld by its pay.
# `why-closed` says so. It used to say why no METHOD stands above ("no field, and the layout is of no class"), which hid the cause.
